1
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:13,760
me

2
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,760
I remember the day after the rain,
when it felt like someone was calling out,

3
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:32,620
me, walking home.

4
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:38,340
Just leave it to Gā-chan,
that feeling I had back then

5
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,960
was such a strange feeling.

6
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

7
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,460
I tried walking only on the black ones.

8
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

9
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,740
but everyone has forgotten.

10
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,780
Politicians with their self-important faces,

11
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:09,100
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too,

12
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,080
come and turn this way.

13
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:14,660
Around that corner.

14
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

15
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,500
Over there is Kameari.

16
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,800
Surely, Kameari is there.

17
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come to our town!

18
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you.

19
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,680
Reiko Akimoto's couple's manzai

20
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,100
Couple's manzai?

21
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,700
Me and Reiko-san?

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,360
No way, I can't do that, Chief!

23
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:52,660
It's the annual entertainment for the
Katsushika Police Station anniversary party.

24
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:56,280
Don't overthink it so stiffly.
Just do it casually.

25
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,440
Calling it
"entertainment" is rather offensive.

26
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:03,560
My manzai with my subordinate at the
anniversary party is already a tradition.

27
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,220
What the heck is that?

28
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,120
Stop it.

29
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,680
That's not right, is it?

30
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:11,980
The natural-born airhead
Terai and the goofball

31
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:15,200
Ryotsu, whose pro-level tsukkomi
shines through high-tech comedy

32
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:18,780
Looking forward to the once-a-year
manzai of the Ryotsu-Terai duo

33
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:22,780
Many officers even bring their parents
and siblings over from their hometowns.

34
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,040
Glasses, glasses!

35
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:31,060
If it were the Kōhaku, our act, which
has reached the level of Sachiko Kobayashi,

36
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:34,760
Please don't call it
"entertainment," not even if your mouth is torn apart, Chief.

37
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,560
What's this doing in a place like this?

38
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,800
A stylish pair of glasses Terai-kun.

39
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,060
Come on, Ryo-san, this is a bucket.

40
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,280
Right.

41
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,780
You two are perfectly in sync.

42
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:48,620
As expected.

43
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,580
That was just a light warm-up.

44
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,960
Sometimes the straight man
turns into the funny man,

45
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:57,620
and when Terai plays straight man,
our teamwork is endlessly versatile.

46
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,680
But on the other hand,

47
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,320
Director

48
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:01,380
Sensei

49
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:07,780
You two have received many complaints that your manzai is vulgar and lacks dignity,
you know.

50
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:11,600
I keep saying we should stop with the dirty jokes,
because they're embarrassing.

51
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,880
Ryo, aren't you running
out of material by now?

52
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:18,920
I'm not resorting to dirty
jokes because I'm out of material.

53
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:22,400
With the executives' stiff, forced greetings
and long-winded congratulatory speeches,

54
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:27,660
the audience's heads are frozen solid. Dirty jokes
are the most effective way to warm them up instantly.

55
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:32,440
That's why I deliberately and actively bring in
dirty jokes to win over the audience's hearts.

56
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:34,300
Please take back what you said.

57
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,720
W-, all right.

58
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:39,980
Sorry, Ryo-san. I had no idea you'd
thought things through that far.

59
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,300
I had no idea at all.

60
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,500
I can't put up with you anymore.
We're ending the partnership!

61
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,520
Thank goodness.

62
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,740
Don't get relieved yet.

63
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,460
Your everyday conversation is
already turning into manzai.

64
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,780
As expected of a veteran,
you really are different.

65
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:57,440
No matter how much money you have piled up,
you can't buy this: the audience's laughter.

66
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:01,700
You two, who've never known hardship,
could never do manzai.

67
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:04,520
Ryo-chan,
don't you think that's a bit harsh?

68
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:07,820
So can you two really do manzai?

69
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,360
I'm not saying you two can't perform.

70
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:14,040
What could these two possibly do?

71
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:17,960
These two are making a joke of comedy
and treating manzai like a joke.

72
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,180
That's not true.

73
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:22,000
Making people laugh is a wonderful job.

74
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,920
So you'll do it, then?

75
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:28,100
Good, good.
I'll register you as performers right away.

76
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:32,300
With you two performing,
the event will be much more glamorous.

77
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:37,880
If you two disgrace the name of the
Kōen-mae police box that we built up,

78
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,160
you'll be in big trouble.

79
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:43,760
Looks like we really are going to do manzai.

80
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,760
What should we do to prepare?

81
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:47,760
I have no idea at all.

82
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:57,940
To protect the citizens from crime
that grows more vicious year after year,

83
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:02,060
we need the wisdom and strength
of each and every one of you.

84
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,400
Something like this happened the other day.

85
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,040
The chief's been talking for
over thirty minutes already.

86
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,720
We're almost up, so please look after us.

87
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,380
Leave it to me.

88
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:15,980
Baseball season's here

89
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:19,020
Yes, I love baseball.

90
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,540
Warm up your shoulders and grit
your teeth through the burn.

91
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,460
Ryo-san & Reiko-san.

92
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,280
Yes!

93
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,880
You two go on after Ryo-chan and the others.

94
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:30,920
Understood.

95
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:35,140
What do we do, Kei-chan?
I really can't do this.

96
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,660
We can't run away now.

97
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,560
Hmph, don't worry.

98
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,496
We'll

99
00:05:40,546 --> 00:05:45,480
go warm up the audience that the
chief's speech has frozen below zero.

100
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:47,502
Now then, everyone,
the moment you've all been waiting for:

101
00:05:47,552 --> 00:05:49,920
here are Ryo-chan and Terai!

102
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:52,680
Hah!

103
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,220
I'm Ryo-chan.

104
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:56,120
And I'm Terai.

105
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,520
Pleased to meet you.

106
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:05,220
Well, we just have to let them
see the results of our practice.

107
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,280
Just endure it for today.

108
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:13,180
So that means Ryo-san went
in and didn't flush, right?

109
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,540
I flushed.

110
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:18,080
I've kept quiet until now,
but I actually have a witness.

111
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,160
A witness?

112
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,560
Just between us.

113
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:23,920
I saw the Chief rushing into the toilet
with his knees together right after me.

114
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,600
The Chief did?

115
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:28,440
No way.

116
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,420
I'm terribly sorry.

117
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,740
The Chief is the one who can
clear my name of suspicion,

118
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,300
since he's both the only
witness and the suspect.

119
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,700
Ryo-san, don't say such things.

120
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:40,080
You'll get transferred to
that remote police box again.

121
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,760
Chief, let's just let this
go and forget about it.

122
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,320
Thank you so much.

123
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,040
Aaaaaah!

124
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:59,420
Are you nervous, Ryo-chan? I heard that if you write the character for
"person" on your palm and swallow it, you won't freeze, so I'm doing it too. I-I'm...

125
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:09,000
Why would you swallow it? It's the character for
"person," not... Next up is you two. Did the audience warm up, or are they frozen solid again?

126
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,080
Hey, Ryo-san,
there's no need to scare us, is there?

127
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,080
Good luck!

128
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,340
Next, we have Ryo-chan & Reiko!

129
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:18,440
Please welcome them
with a round of applause!

130
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,360
Ryo-chan & Reiko!

131
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,340
Reiko-san!

132
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,631
H-hello,

133
00:07:28,681 --> 00:07:31,500
Hello, we're Ryo-chan &...

134
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,900
I-I'm Reiko!

135
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,320
K-k-k-k-k...

136
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,900
R-r-Ryo-chan?

137
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:43,600
Has anything interesting happened lately?

138
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:49,640
I've had so much fun every day, so much fun!

139
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,960
What's so fun about it?

140
00:07:52,960 --> 00:08:01,140
Well, Ryo-san,
you got laughs again this year.

141
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,100
Well, it's all thanks to my talent.

142
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,360
Thank you for your hard work.

143
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:08,140
This gentleman said he has
something to discuss with you.

144
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,740
Nice to meet you, I'm with this company.

145
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,240
Event producer.

146
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:22,680
We'd really like you two to take part
in the next Asakusa Manzai Contest.

147
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,920
Contest?

148
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,240
Don't tell me this is a scouting offer?

149
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,940
The Asakusa Manzai Contest is the gateway for young,
up-and-coming manzai comedians.

150
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:37,520
It's broadcast on TV too, so if you win, you
could become a nationally known face overnight.

151
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:51,740
Yes, you're well informed. To celebrate the contest's 30th anniversary,
we've been recruiting entrants to discover new talent for a new era of manzai, but something still feels lacking.

152
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:59,720
But today, I happened to stop by this Katsushika station to renew my license,
and by sheer chance I got to see your manzai.

153
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:07,360
I see, it's truly a fateful meeting. I shouldn't say this too loudly,
but you're the favorites to win.

154
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,500
You'll perform, won't you?

155
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:11,700
Of course!

156
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,420
Hold on, Ryo-san.

157
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:16,580
Our manzai is just a hobby, after all.

158
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,240
There's no way we can do TV.

159
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:18,800
What?

160
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:23,160
Didn't you hear that manzai just now?

161
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,220
Our manzai has already
gone beyond a mere hobby.

162
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,940
But most of the audience are people we know,

163
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:31,000
and our material isn't
only crowd-pleasing jokes.

164
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:32,160
You know.

165
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:35,140
Are you saying my material
won't work anywhere else?

166
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,480
That's a stretch.

167
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,880
I write manzai scripts with
a specific audience in mind.

168
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,580
So for Alaska,
I write for Alaskan audiences,

169
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:47,600
and for Egypt, I write manzai that
makes Egyptian audiences laugh.

170
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:51,740
If we're performing in Katsushika, I'll plant
material that makes Katsushika audiences laugh.

171
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,440
Okay, okay, just tell me already.

172
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:01,700
Why were you even born into this world,
with no redeeming qualities at all?

173
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,940
It's so you can be the straight man
getting roasted by my jokes in our manzai.

174
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,060
Fulfill your destiny!

175
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,940
That's ridiculous, Ryo-san.

176
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:13,820
Wow, as expected of a great duo,
how wonderful.

177
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,920
By the way,
how much is the contest prize money?

178
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:20,840
For this kind of contest,
it's an unusually generous 3 million yen.

179
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:23,420
3 million yen!?

180
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:26,700
Extra income like this is a blessing right now,
isn't it, Terai?

181
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,327
Your home loan,

182
00:10:28,377 --> 00:10:30,800
you've still got 30 years left on it, right?

183
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:38,260
To give it as a present to my my boyfriend
(the Japanese is garbled; intended meaning: "To give as a present to him, the one who got burned")

184
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,820
I've been knitting.

185
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,400
Knitting

186
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:43,020
What are you doing?

187
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,100
One, two, three!

188
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:46,600
I'm done, I made it!

189
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,760
Ryo-san, I'll do it.

190
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,840
Alright, it's settled.

191
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,380
Then, I'll accept this offer

192
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,400
Thank you very much.

193
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,100
Thank you very much.

194
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,900
Thanks to that fly, it was a total disaster.

195
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:07,320
I don't want to do it again, either.

196
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,520
No, no, no, no, it went over big, didn't it?

197
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:13,300
It wasn't like that at all.

198
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:16,240
If there hadn't been a fly,
we could have done it properly.

199
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:19,020
After all that practice,
it's so frustrating.

200
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,860
These two performed on stage
for the first time today.

201
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:31,380
They're just amateurs, so please forgive them.
To fire up the audience like that on their first stage...

202
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:36,200
Ryo-san, Terai-san, I'm so sorry!

203
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:41,000
Ryo-chan and Reiko-san,
please do enter the contest!

204
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:44,440
Wh-what?!

205
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:52,512
Putting people on stage who don't even
know the first thing about manzai timing,

206
00:11:52,562 --> 00:11:56,360
the Asakusa manzai contest
has really hit rock bottom.

207
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:02,440
The contest wasn't even planned to begin with,
you know.

208
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:04,480
Cheer up, Ryo-san.

209
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,720
Shut up. It was you who

210
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:09,260
should have just said
yes right away back then.

211
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:12,140
A chance like this, and you'd hand it
over to the likes of Nakagawa and Reiko!

212
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:15,100
Senpai, we're going to decline.

213
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:21,460
We're not even aspiring manzai performers,
after all.

214
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,680
There's no point in us entering the contest.

215
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,220
What a wasteful thing to say!

216
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,260
Three million yen, that's three million.

217
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:30,140
First prize is 3 million yen.

218
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,560
Ryo-san.

219
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:35,660
Saying that to two
billionaires is pointless.

220
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:40,140
Damn it, it's so frustrating, like
scratching at my little toe through my shoe.

221
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,120
Why doesn't the senior
officer go in our place?

222
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:47,300
Yeah, that's what it was
supposed to be at first, right?

223
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:51,540
If you could do that, I wouldn't
be expecting anything from you two.

224
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:54,500
Ryo-san, you beat that producer to a pulp,
didn't you?

225
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:57,420
We got banned from the contest.

226
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,360
After working so hard on our manzai, too.

227
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,340
How pitiful.

228
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:03,880
Don't worry.

229
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:08,380
Before the contest, I'll turn you
two into proper manzai performers.

230
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,908
Nakagawa, Reiko,

231
00:13:10,958 --> 00:13:14,600
I'll pass on everything I know to you,
holding nothing back.

232
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,880
W-wait a minute, Ryo-chan.

233
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:20,400
Good sailing weather comes to those who wait.
Heaven hasn't abandoned me after all.

234
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:23,660
Ever since that day,
when I was still in Mom's belly,

235
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,800
the variety hall I used to visit so often,

236
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,980
Kenichi Enomoto, Roppa Furukawa,

237
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,240
Kamigata manzai's Entatsu and Achako,

238
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,480
Senpai, we have no intention
of entering the contest.

239
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:35,840
It's no use, he won't listen to a word.

240
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,420
What do we do, Reiko-san?

241
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,260
If we refuse, I'm scared of what comes next.

242
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:42,640
Who knows what kind of harassment we'll get.

243
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,320
Please!

244
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:46,880
I've loved manzai so much,

245
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:50,120
so please clear my regret
for loving Asakusa, Reiko.

246
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,480
Ryo-chan, okay, I get it already.

247
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,080
Just this once, got it?

248
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,560
You'll do it? Thanks.

249
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:03,220
Alright, no matter what,
I'll make these two win

250
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:06,020
and get that 3 million yen prize money.

251
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,640
Listen, from today on, I'm your master.

252
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,400
Never talk back to what your master says.

253
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:16,960
If I say black, then mailboxes
and bananas are all black too.

254
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:17,740
Understood?

255
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:19,080
Y-yes.

256
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,140
I hate dressing like this.

257
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:23,300
Me too.

258
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:25,960
We only have one week until the contest.

259
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,360
We'll go with practical training here.

260
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,620
First, I'll show you an example.

261
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,300
Yes.

262
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:39,240
Keep your hips low and stretch your arms out,
like you're chasing a chicken.

263
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:42,140
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

264
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:43,780
Give it a try.

265
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:45,280
This is embarrassing.

266
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:48,720
Couldn't we do this somewhere
with less foot traffic, senpai?

267
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,940
Call me master. Master.

268
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:52,380
Master.

269
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:55,800
If you're too embarrassed,
you'll never be able to make people laugh.

270
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,240
Just do it already.

271
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:17,740
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes,
yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

272
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:18,720
Kin-chan run!

273
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:22,360
Why does it turn out like this?
Why does it turn out like this?

274
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:23,380
Alright, let's give it a try!

275
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:25,560
Welcome back!

276
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:28,720
So, you've gained a little nerve,
haven't you?

277
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:32,600
Well, I'm off on patrol now,
so take care of things.

278
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:37,280
Everyday comedy is a constant
stream of boke and tsukkomi.

279
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,360
Well, first let's have
some tea and take a break.

280
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,920
First, boil some water.

281
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:46,360
What's the point of just gaping at the boke?

282
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:48,080
That's the one, right?

283
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:52,240
Even a lame pun can get a laugh with
just one tsukkomi from your partner.

284
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,500
When your partner plays the fool,
jump in with a tsukkomi right away.

285
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:55,080
Yes.

286
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,500
Alright, let's start from the beginning.

287
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,020
First, boil some water in the kettle.

288
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,860
This kettle doesn't have a lid!

289
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:03,520
And this is a bucket, isn't it!

290
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:04,940
Nice one, Reiko!

291
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:07,300
When did you learn nori-tsukkomi?

292
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,160
Is this right?

293
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,860
That's the spirit,
don't be afraid, keep coming at me!

294
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:12,140
Yes.

295
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:16,300
Now, put the tea leaves into the teapot.

296
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,380
Too fast!

297
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:22,740
Oops.

298
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:25,260
I went and did a tsukkomi
when there was no boke!

299
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:26,400
Nakagawa.

300
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:29,020
You panicked,
thinking Reiko had gotten ahead of you.

301
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,760
Focus on your partner's words and actions.

302
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,160
Yes.

303
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,660
This is bad, this is bad!

304
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:36,800
It's bad.

305
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,260
What's wrong, Terai?

306
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:42,180
Terai.

307
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:45,520
When did you get so big without me noticing?

308
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:46,920
That's a utility pole.

309
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:48,460
This is no time for that!

310
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:51,580
A kiss at 3-chome!

311
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:54,180
A kiss? Come on, Terai-san!

312
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:54,980
Ugh...

313
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:57,520
That's enough!

314
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,840
Alright, let's head out!

315
00:16:58,840 --> 00:16:59,680
Yes.

316
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,040
Let's go.

317
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:05,400
Chances to boke are lying around everywhere.

318
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,080
Yes.

319
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:07,360
Keep up!

320
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,420
Go ahead.

321
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:16,060
Please, go easy on us.

322
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,860
Welcome!

323
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:27,360
Next, the rookie manzai detective
duo Meon will be your opponents.

324
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,340
What?

325
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,520
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

326
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:36,080
Then let me inspect that bag right away.

327
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:38,840
Just let us inspect it, come on.

328
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:41,160
If we don't inspect it, then that...

329
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:43,040
Then, pardon me.

330
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,180
What a nice bag!

331
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:47,100
Where did you buy it?

332
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,760
T-this was a gift from someone.

333
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,600
I see, so it's a present

334
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:54,060
So what, you're just going to accept it?

335
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:57,200
Even if someone gave it to you,
didn't you just quietly take it?

336
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,560
N-no, nothing like that...

337
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,760
Then, excuse me,
let's take a look inside your bag.

338
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,600
Well, that's a bit much.

339
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,340
Then, no thanks.

340
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,980
You give up too quickly.

341
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:08,420
Here, we push push forcefully.

342
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,220
Push push.

343
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,860
That's not the right kind of push.

344
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:14,020
Push push.

345
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:16,260
So what's the point of pushing?

346
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,140
That's not it. I said do it harder.

347
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,540
Harder! It's a press!

348
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:25,680
I told you, don't push!

349
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,940
Sorry, this is like
leaving a snake half-dead.

350
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:35,220
Just arrest me already, hurry up and do it.
What a wealthy man you are.

351
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:38,200
I told you, I'm the culprit. Now arrest me!

352
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:42,220
Yes. Oh no, I forgot the handcuffs.

353
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:45,320
Then you can't make the arrest!
Please wait a moment.

354
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:46,480
Yes.

355
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,480
Found them.

356
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,680
Then let's hurry up and make the arrest.

357
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,840
Arrest!

358
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:54,520
Octopus.

359
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,320
How are we supposed to
arrest anyone with this?

360
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,620
I said, just grab them with
the suction cup and, zip!

361
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:02,240
There's no way we can
catch anyone with this.

362
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,540
Hurry up and bring it here.

363
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:04,020
Yes.

364
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,640
Hey, don't go!

365
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,300
It's fine, I'll be right back.

366
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:10,840
I got it.

367
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:13,540
Why did you bring a squid, anyway?

368
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,740
It's just a squid, so hurry up and catch it!

369
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,360
Ever since the sudden cutoff, nonstop...

370
00:19:21,300 --> 00:19:23,020
Somehow I feel lighter,

371
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:26,880
and tsukkomi lines well up
naturally from the bottom of my heart.

372
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:28,180
It was a strange feeling.

373
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:32,020
It was as if the fog before
me had suddenly cleared,

374
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:34,300
and I could come up with
one bit after another.

375
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:37,380
You endured these five
days of training well,

376
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:40,060
and you have mastered boke
and tsukkomi splendidly.

377
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:43,560
Master, this is...

378
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:50,420
the script of honor and manzai I've kept for years,
for when I'd find a partner for life.

379
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:55,180
Since I don't seem to be getting a stage for a while,
I've decided to give it to you two.

380
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:58,180
Something so precious, to us?

381
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:03,660
It's packed with bits that
Asakusa audiences would love.

382
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:07,680
Breathe life into it in my place.

383
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,620
Master

384
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:15,000
We appreciate it,
but we can't accept this script.

385
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,440
Reiko-san, how can you say that
without even reading the script?

386
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:23,580
If we performed it,
it would surely be a borrowed Asakusa

387
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:26,500
it would only be a borrowed manzai, I think.

388
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:29,800
That's why we want to write our own script.

389
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,220
Sorry for being so selfish.

390
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:38,240
If you're that determined,
go ahead and try it yourselves.

391
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:40,880
But the contest is the day after tomorrow,
you know.

392
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:41,960
How much time do we have?

393
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:43,900
We still have two days.

394
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,840
The two of us will create our own manzai.

395
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:49,740
Understood.

396
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:50,400
Yeah.

397
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,460
A great manzai duo
Translation>
always has its own individuality.

398
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:56,600
always has its own individuality.

399
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:59,420
Your own individuality,

400
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:00,920
go find it.

401
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,820
Our own individuality...

402
00:21:02,820 --> 00:21:04,640
We'll definitely find it.

403
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,220
Nakagawa and the others are late,
aren't they.

404
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:16,540
Did they get scared after all?

405
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:18,580
Those two will definitely come.

406
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:21,740
I believe in those guys' performer spirit.

407
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:24,080
Those police officers,
they're something else.

408
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:48,040
Ah, hey!

409
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:49,740
Master!

410
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:51,400
What's with that getup?

411
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:54,700
We've found our individuality.

412
00:21:55,160 --> 00:22:00,140
We realized we're the richest, most handsome
and beautiful manzai duo in the world!

413
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:05,640
We'll try showing our individuality
to the audience in Asakusa.

414
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:07,520
Au revoir, Master.

415
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:09,840
Aaaaaah!

416
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:16,500
No good. That'll only earn the audience's ill will.
My 3 million yen...

417
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:22,460
We three aren't allowed in the venue, are we?
Let's watch the TV together at the police box.

418
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:28,520
Gap-shi, you stay inside and keep an eye on them.
I'm going to go play pachinko and head home.

419
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:34,140
What, we won first place?

420
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:36,800
The two of you did a
masterpiece of a manzai.

421
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:38,980
You should have watched it too, Ryo-san.

422
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:41,140
Here's the first-place prize money.

423
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:44,100
This is for me?

424
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:45,540
It's a thank-you for coaching us.

425
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:48,140
Now I can get back to my
police duties without a worry.

426
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:51,580
Wow, it's even in the newspaper,
and this big!

427
00:22:51,980 --> 00:22:55,220
Good for you, Ryo-san. All your
wishes have come true, haven't they?

428
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:57,960
So, what kind of manzai
did you two actually perform?

429
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:05,000
Just thinking about it makes me
laugh so hard I can't even explain it.

430
00:23:05,340 --> 00:23:07,660
Good morning, good morning!

431
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:13,260
Stop it, don't make me laugh.

432
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:18,700
I watched your manzai on TV yesterday,
and I laughed so hard my stomach twisted up.

433
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:21,400
I nearly called an ambulance!

434
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:25,020
Chief, did you watch these two's manzai too?

435
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:26,900
Why didn't you watch it, Ryo-san?

436
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:29,640
You didn't see that?

437
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:32,300
The one from Nishi-Shinjuku?

438
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,540
The hectopascal one?

439
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:37,740
Are you peeling onions?

440
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:40,480
W-what is it?

441
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,960
What happened with the
onions in Nishi-Shinjuku?

442
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:46,900
Nakagawa, Renko, show me that manzai too.

443
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:47,780
B-but...

444
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,100
Please, I'll give you this 3 million yen.

445
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,960
If I don't see it, I'll die with regrets.

446
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:55,080
What kind of manzai did you actually do?

447
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:58,400
Please, just let me see it too.

448
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:05,540
Kick the alarm clock away,
ouch, my little toe!

449
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:13,960
Draw on my eyebrows in a hurry,
then dash, dash, dash to the station!

450
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:19,440
Packed train, a nap on some old man's back.

451
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:25,720
Another hard week, overwork,
you're absolutely right.

452
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,560
Holding a bucket in one hand,
looking all composed.

453
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:33,380
Beef bowl, extra sauce, cloudy and soupy.

454
00:24:33,380 --> 00:24:36,640
The irritation from endless overtime,

455
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:40,240
gets cleared right up by more irritation.

456
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:46,140
Every day is no-profe...

457
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:16,120
Thank you for watching.

458
00:25:20,380 --> 00:25:21,240
It's not like that.

459
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:24,280
I wasn't a real taxi, I was staking out

460
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:26,580
You're giving me this much?

461
00:25:26,580 --> 00:25:29,340
This is way better than being a cop!

462
00:25:30,020 --> 00:25:33,160
Alright, if it's come to this,
I'm switching careers to taxi driver!

463
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:36,240
Next time: Ryotsu Taxi,
now open for business!

464
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:37,460
See you then.

465
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,840
That's Kameari over there.

466
00:25:41,900 --> 00:25:44,960
Well, it's surely Kameari.

467
00:25:46,140 --> 00:25:49,200
Everyone, come on over to our town!

468
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:50,860
Thank you.

